# Django ORM Patterns for Nautobot:
- Always use Nautobot's base model classes instead of Django's base Model class:
  * Use `PrimaryModel` from `nautobot.apps.models` for standard models
  * Reference Nautobot documentation for choosing the right base model: https://docs.nautobot.com/projects/core/en/stable/plugins/development/#database-models
- Use Nautobot constants for field lengths:
  * Import and use `CHARFIELD_MAX_LENGTH` from `nautobot.apps.constants` for CharField max_length
- Use the `extras_features` decorator from `nautobot.apps.models` to enable Nautobot features:
  * Common features: "custom_links", "custom_validators", "export_templates", "graphql", "webhooks"
  * Reference: https://docs.nautobot.com/projects/core/en/stable/development/core/model-checklist/#extras-features
- For API views, use `NautobotModelViewSet` from `nautobot.apps.api` instead of Django REST Framework's ModelViewSet
- For UI views, use `NautobotUIViewSet` from `nautobot.apps.views` instead of standard Django views
- For API serializers, use `NautobotModelSerializer` and `TaggedModelSerializerMixin` from `nautobot.apps.api`
- For filtering, use `NautobotFilterSet` and `NameSearchFilterSet` from `nautobot.apps.filters`
- Always use queryset pattern: `models.ModelName.objects.all()` in viewsets
- Follow Nautobot's Meta class patterns with proper ordering and verbose names
- Implement `__str__` method that returns a meaningful string representation (typically the name field)
- Use proper field relationships (ForeignKey, ManyToManyField) following Nautobot conventions
- When creating migrations, use Django's standard migration commands but ensure they follow Nautobot's model structure

